      "arm": "leaks-the-path",
      "impl": "node",
      "file": "src/document.ts",
      "why": "the response carries the filesystem path it read from, under the key the app reads as a reference. The first spelling of this arm ADDED a `path` field and tsc refused it: `images` is typed `Array<{reference; media; base64}>` and an object literal carrying an extra property is an excess-property error. So the type already forbids the leak by addition and says nothing about the leak by substitution \u2014 which is the one the wire assertion is here to catch.",
      "scenarioExpectedRed": "escape, served",
      "verdict": "red",
      "detail": "red exactly where declared: escape, served",
